---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Join & contact"><section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="prose"><p class="kicker">Come by</p><h1>Join & contact</h1><p class="lede">You do not need an invitation or a particular kind of math background. Show up to a social, bring a question to a lunch discussion, volunteer at an outreach event, or just write to us.</p><h2>Ways to get involved</h2><ul><li><strong>Come to an event.</strong> The chapter organizes monthly socials, lunch discussions, workshops, speakers, and study sessions.</li><li><strong>Find a mentor.</strong> Undergraduate and graduate students can connect through the <a href={`${base}programs/mentoring`}>mentoring program</a>.</li><li><strong>Help with outreach.</strong> The <a href={`${base}programs/outreach`}>outreach program</a> works with schools and community partners.</li><li><strong>Volunteer.</strong> Since 2019, the chapter has worked through committees. <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc6ZMFcBZbZxoWAtxd0Azca6-EAqyrSEmmZmpl57ZJX2I1FDQ/viewform">Fill out the volunteer form</a>.</li><li><strong>Keep up with the chapter.</strong> Find AWM on <a href="https://getinvolved.utah.edu/organization/awm-utah">Campus Connect</a>, <a href="https://www.facebook.com/UofUAWM/">Facebook</a>, and <a href="https://www.instagram.com/uofuawm/">Instagram</a>.</li><li><strong>Chapter history.</strong> Browse the <a href={`${base}archive/merchandise/`}>archived merchandise page</a>; it is preserved as historical information, not a current sales page.</li></ul><h2>Contact the chapter</h2><p>For information, suggestions, or just to talk, email <a href="mailto:uofuAWM@math.utah.edu">uofuAWM@math.utah.edu</a>.</p><p>Department of Mathematics, JWB 233<br />155 S 1400 E<br />Salt Lake City, UT 84112<br />Phone: <a href="tel:+18015816851">(801) 581-6851</a></p><h2>Accessibility requests</h2><p>Email us before an event if you have access questions or need an accommodation. We will work with you and the University to support participation.</p></div></div></section></BaseLayout>
